<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Dries Q1 pre-capex net profit falls.</title>
<headline>Dries Q1 pre-capex net profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-March versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit before capital spending  182.02 vs 214.09</p>
<p>    Capital spending			  132.13 vs 162.58</p>
<p>Full name: Driefontein Consolidated Ltd, managed by Gold Fields of South Africa Ltd  </p>
<p>Gold output (kg)</p>
<p>    East Dries-		    6,354.2	 vs 5,754.0</p>
<p>    West Dries-		    5,784.9	 vs 5,478.1</p>
<p>    Reclamation plant-	   83.2	    vs   241.5</p>
<p>Tonnes milled/treated</p>
<p>    East Dries-		     640,000	vs 647,000</p>
<p>    West Dries-		     694,000	vs 661,000</p>
<p>    Reclamation plant-	    430,000	vs 589,000</p>
<p>Yield (gram/t)</p>
<p>    East Dries-		     9.9	    vs 8.9</p>
<p>    West Dries-		     8.3	    vs 8.3</p>
<p>    Reclamation plant-	    0.2	    vs 0.4</p>
<p>Cost (rand/kg)</p>
<p>    East Dries-		     31,752	 vs 32,920</p>
<p>    West Dries-		     39,169	 vs 40,332</p>
<p>Revenue (rand/kg)</p>
<p>    East Dries-		     51,954	 vs 56,414</p>
<p>    West Dries-		     51,612	 vs 56,224</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it expected to maintain gold output in the next quarter.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482-1003</p>
